{
  "scope": "Real full tick; native Canvas and browser DOM stubbed; frames of 1/64 s; a desk of 1440×900 (the stories at 1900×810); the worker of Wings headless thinking sixteen rehearsed frames a frame. With Apace's rule taken out and no budget, the tour and the chain through every page from every other are Cohort's, the world and every drawing command, frame by frame. With the rule alone (no budget) over the tour and the chain, the cells have less far to go when the hive turns crisp than on Cohort, and the seeds lag their plans less when their clocks run out. On the chain and the tour nothing waits, nothing fractures, from each round that moved a cell the performance is that round's rehearsal of the move to the bit, every change has one pace, every page at rest is exact and every cell drawn its own colour. With no worker the hive thinks on the page and plays what it rehearsed. In a Cue story the rule does nothing: every frame of it is the same with it switched off as it begins; a Tell and a Tell II story run to their end and home without a fractured cell. Defects and the screen leaned on are reported against Cohort.",
